   101	
   102	**KBM's approach.** KBM's project coordination has not articulated a formal resource-and-capacity-management framework; resource management has been handled informally by PMs.
   103	
   104	**Pivot's approach.** Pivot's BRD articulates resource allocation and capacity management as a Workfront capability — assigning resources to project tasks, tracking capacity utilization, balancing workloads across PMs and field service.
   105	
   106	**Recommendation for the merged company.** Adopt Pivot's resource allocation and capacity management framework, built in Orion's project module with custom enhancements during the Workfront sunset transition. The framework provides the merged company with capacity visibility that KBM has not had previously, and preserves the operating discipline Pivot's PMs already rely on.
   107	
   108	**Decision for the leadership team.** Confirm: Pivot's resource allocation and capacity management framework adopted as merged-company default, built in Orion native per D-1. *Recommended default: yes.*
   109	
   110	---
   111	
   112	### D-5. Project status visibility and dashboards
   113	
   114	**Source:** Pivot project-status dashboard sections; cross-references BI §3.09 D-4 (360 dashboards including Project Performance 360)
   115	
   116	**KBM's approach.** KBM articulates project-level KPI dashboards within BI §3.09 D-4 (Project Performance 360 dashboard).
   117	
   118	**Pivot's approach.** Pivot articulates project-status dashboards in Workfront with status, milestone, timeline, and resource visibility, plus separate Project Performance 360 dashboard within NetSuite for financial KPIs (per BI §3.09 D-4).
   119	
   120	**Recommendation for the merged company.** Operate the merged company with NetSuite Orion as the system of record for both project financial KPIs (Project Performance 360 dashboard per BI §3.09 D-4) and project execution status (timeline, milestones, resource utilization). Execution-status and financial-status dashboards both reside in Orion after the Workfront sunset. Custom enhancements deliver the execution-visibility depth Pivot's PMs rely on today.
   121	
   122	**Decision for the leadership team.** Confirm: NetSuite Orion as system of record for project financial KPIs and project execution status. *Recommended default: yes.*
   123	
   124	---
   125	
   126	## 3.06.4 Cross-area dependencies
   127	
   128	| Dependency | Where it surfaced in Project Management | Where it's decided |
   129	|---|---|---|
   130	| **Project record framework (financial KPIs)** | D-2 | **BI (§3.09 D-4)** — Project Performance 360 dashboard locked; **Financial Management (§3.08)** — project accounting decided there |
   131	| **IPM and sales-coordinator routing** | D-3 | **Pre-Quote (§3.03 D-8)** — routing model locked; Project Management uses the model |
   132	| **Time tracking (project-GP impact)** | Time tracking against project tasks | **Operations (§3.05 D-7)** — time tracking framework decided |
   133	| **Document storage architecture** | Project documentation, contracts, drawings | **System Setup & Configuration (§3.10 D-3)** |
   134	| **Multi-company / multi-contact relationship model** | Project-level customer / vendor / influencer relationships | **CRM (§3.02 D-4)** — relationship model locked |
   135	| **GP framework (actual vs. commissionable)** | Project profitability reporting | **CRM (§3.02 D-6)** — GP framework locked |
   136	| **Workfront sunset and data migration** | Project, task, time, and capacity data migration from Workfront to Orion native | **System Setup & Configuration (§3.10 D-5)** — historical data migration scope; transition plan owned in Project Management D-1 |
   137	
   138	## 3.06.5 Recommendation summary
   139	
   140	The merged-company Project Management playbook in shorthand:
   141	
   142	- **Platform architecture:** NetSuite Orion native project record consolidation; Workfront sunsets on a defined transition timeline
   143	- **Project record:** NetSuite Orion native project record as financial-and-reporting aggregation layer and project-execution system of record
   144	- **Role taxonomy:** IPM-and-sales-coordinator routing per Pivot framework; KBM staff role assignments during organizational alignment
   145	- **Resource allocation and capacity management:** Pivot framework adopted, built in Orion native with custom enhancements during the Workfront sunset transition
   146	- **Project status dashboards:** NetSuite Orion for both project financial KPIs (Project Performance 360 per BI §3.09 D-4) and project execution status
   147	- **Time tracking:** Per Operations §3.05 D-7 framework; feeds dual GP and project profitability
   148	
   149	Net read: project management is the most operationally significant transition in the unification because Pivot's PMs work primarily in Workfront today. The recommendation commits to Orion-native consolidation in line with Pivot's own BRD direction; the working-session decisions are about transition shape — capability-replacement scope at cutover, sunset timeline, and Pivot PM team migration plan — not about whether Workfront is retained.
   150	
   151	## 3.06.6 Decisions for the leadership team
   152	
   153	| # | Decision | Default | Reference |
   154	|---|---|---|---|
   155	| 1a | Project management consolidates into NetSuite Orion native; Workfront sunsets on a defined transition timeline | Yes | D-1 |
   156	| 1b | Capability-replacement scope at cutover and Workfront sunset timeline | Refine at working session with Pivot PM team input | D-1 |
   157	| 2 | NetSuite Orion native project record as merged-company financial-and-reporting aggregation layer and project-execution system of record | Yes | D-2 |
   158	| 3 | Pivot's resource allocation and capacity management framework adopted, built in Orion native (cross-references Operations §3.05 D-8 scheduling/resource management) | Yes | D-4 |
   159	| 4 | NetSuite Orion as system of record for project financial KPIs and project execution status | Yes | D-5 |
   160	
   161	> 5 decisions: 4 with default-yes recommendations and 1 (decision 1b, transition shape) refined at the working session with Pivot PM team input. The platform-consolidation direction is committed; the working-session focus is the transition plan that protects Pivot PM productivity through cutover. (D-3 IPM-and-sales-coordinator routing is inherited from Pre-Quote §3.03 D-8 and does not require a separate decision here.)
   162	
   163	## 3.06.7 Configuration carryover
   164	
   165	| Item | KBM-side built? | Pivot-side built? | Action for merged company |
   166	|---|---|---|---|
   167	| Dedicated project-management platform | Not built (no platform) | Workfront in production | Sunset Workfront per D-1 transition plan; Orion native is the merged-company platform |
   168	| NetSuite Orion native project record | In progress | In progress | Configure per D-2 as financial aggregation layer and execution system of record |
   169	| Workfront sunset and data migration | N/A | Workfront in production | Plan migration of project, task, time, and capacity data per D-1; align with System Setup §3.10 D-5 |
   170	| IPM role taxonomy | Not present | Present | Adopt per D-3 |
   171	| Resource allocation and capacity management | Not built | Built in Workfront | Build in Orion native per D-4 with custom enhancements during the Workfront sunset transition |
   172	| Project Performance 360 dashboard | Specified per BI §3.09 D-4 | Specified per BI §3.09 D-4 | Build per BI §3.09 |
   173	
   174	## 3.06.8 Open questions / inputs needed
   175	
   176	1. **Capability-replacement scope at cutover** (decision 1b) — which Workfront features must be present in Orion at go-live (task management depth, dependency tracking, resource allocation, capacity management, status dashboards) vs. phased afterward; refined at the working session with Pivot PM team input.
   177	2. **Workfront sunset timeline** (decision 1b) — date for Workfront subscription wind-down and the transition shape that gets the Pivot PM team there without operational disruption; refined at the working session.
   178	3. **KBM staff role assignments** — IPM vs. sales-coordinator categorization for KBM PMs during organizational alignment.
   179	4. **Sherri Nuzum knowledge transfer** — Pivot's Workfront knowledge-holder named in Pre-Quote BRD; knowledge-transfer plan during the Workfront sunset transition documented during change-management planning.
   180	5. **Workfront historical data migration scope** — project, task, time, and capacity data extraction from Workfront and migration to Orion native; planned with System Setup §3.10 D-5.
   181	6. **Custom enhancement design** — task management depth, dependency tracking, and capacity management enhancements documented during Realize-phase design.
   182	7. **Pivot project management stakeholder review** — Pivot project-management leadership reviews merged-company recommendations and the transition plan before the working session.

