_Unification/07 - System Setup & Configuration.md:81:### D-3. Document management and storage architecture
_Unification/07 - System Setup & Configuration.md:83:**Source:** KBM Google Drive integration (Marketing §3.01); Pivot SharePoint integration; cross-references CT-14
_Unification/07 - System Setup & Configuration.md:85:**KBM's approach.** KBM's existing document collaboration uses Google Drive, integrated with NetSuite via the Google Drive connector for opportunity, project, and RFP documents.
_Unification/07 - System Setup & Configuration.md:87:**Pivot's approach.** Pivot's existing document management uses SharePoint, with a SharePoint integration listed as one of the considered SuiteApps.
_Unification/07 - System Setup & Configuration.md:89:**Recommendation for the merged company.** Operate the merged company with NetSuite File Cabinet as the primary document repository for transactional documents (invoices, POs, contracts, signed proposals) and SharePoint as the merged-company collaboration-document platform. KBM's Google Drive content migrates to SharePoint on a defined transition timeline, with the Google Drive integration sunset once migration completes. The recommendation aligns with Pivot's existing operational footprint (SharePoint deployed and integrated into existing workflows), preserves the document-management discipline Pivot's teams already rely on, and removes the integration overhead of maintaining two collaboration platforms long-term. KBM users onboard into SharePoint as part of the Discovery → Activate transition.
_Unification/07 - System Setup & Configuration.md:94:- (3b) Confirm: SharePoint as merged-company collaboration-document platform with KBM Google Drive content migrating on a defined transition timeline. *Recommended default: yes.*
